{"results":[{"url":"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/","final_url":"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/27/fact-check-rumors-hunter-biden-dead-4-chan-hoax/3754066001/","title":"Fact check: False rumors that Hunter Biden is dead are a 4chan hoax","description":"A false rumor that Hunter Biden — the son of former Vice President Joe Biden — has died originated on 4chan.","language":"en","text":"FACT CHECK\n\nfact-checking\n\n# Fact check: False rumors that Hunter Biden is dead are a 4chan hoax\n\nCamille Caldera\n\nUSA TODAY\n\nOct. 27, 2020, 6:49 p.m. ET\n\n## The claim: Hunter Biden died of a drug overdose\n\nRumors that Hunter Biden — the son of former Vice President Joe Biden — has died of an overdose have appeared on Facebook this week.\n\n\"I have unconfirmed reports Hunter Biden has either died from a crack overdose or is in serious condition.... ANYONE have any info on this?\" Elizabeth Sequoria posted.\n\nSequoria declined a request for comment from USA TODAY.\n\n\"Word on the street is Hunter Biden is possibly now dead, apparently from a 'drug overdose,'\" Kat Dekari Zaghi wrote.\n\nOn Instagram, some accounts — including BATEFM and Guntraband — also posted a screenshot of a headline from the site Hollywood News LA that read \"Joe Biden’s Son Hunter Died From Drug Overdose in Suicide Attempt?\"\n\nZaghi, BATEFM, Guntraband and Hollywood News LA have not responded to requests from USA TODAY for comment.\n\n## Hoax about his death originated on 4chan\n\nThere is no proof to support the claim that Hunter Biden is dead. Both Lead Stories and Heavy also concluded that the claim is false.\n\nThe unfounded rumor appears to have started with a post on 4chan, which is archived here. It was posted Oct. 25 on a board titled \"Politically Incorrect.\"\n\n“Hunter Biden died of a crack overdose over 20 minutes ago,\" it reads. \"Joe is already on his way to the hospital.\"\n\nA week before Election Day, reporters in the press pool are appraised of almost every move a presidential candidate like Joe Biden makes.\n\nOn Sunday, Oct. 25, Biden attended church in Wilmington, Delaware, with his granddaughters and appeared at a virtual concert later that night, per the Associated Press.\n\nOn Monday, Oct. 26, he made a surprise appearance in Delaware County, Pennsylvania, per the Philadelphia Inquirer. On Tuesday, Oct. 27, Biden was set to campaign in Georgia, per The Hill.\n\nHunter Biden, by contrast, lives in Los Angeles, per the New York Times. He is a recovering drug addict, something he and his father have been open about.\n\nHunter Biden is also the only surviving child from his father's first marriage. His sister, Naomi, died as an infant in a car crash, alongside his mother, per the Associated Press. His brother, Beau, died in 2015 of brain cancer.\n\n## Our rating: False\n\nBased on our research, the claim that Hunter Biden has died is FALSE. There is no evidence to support it, and it appears to be a hoax that originated on 4chan.\n\n## Our fact-check sources:\n\n* Lead Stories, Oct. 26, Fact Check: NO Evidence That Hunter Biden Is Dead\n* Heavy, Oct. 26, Hunter Biden Is Not Dead: Overdose Story Is a 4chan Death Hoax\n* 4chan, Oct. 25, thread\n* Associated Press, Oct. 25, The Latest: Biden attends church, plans push on early voting\n* Philadelphia Inquirer, Oct. 26, Biden makes surprise stop in Delco; Trump holds 3 rallies in Pa.; Philly residents flock to early voting sites\n* The Hill, Oct. 27, Oct. 27: Where Biden and Trump are campaigning today\n* The New York Times, Feb. 28, There’s a New Artist in Town. The Name Is Biden.\n* Associated Press, Aug. 18, 2019, Biden’s prism of loss: A public man, shaped by private grief\n\n*Thank you for supporting our journalism. You can subscribe to our print edition, ad-free app or electronic newspaper replica here.*\n\n*Our fact check work is supported in part by a grant from Facebook.*\n\n*This fact check is available at IFCN’s 2020 US Elections FactChat #Chatbot on WhatsApp. Click here, for more.*\n\nFeatured Weekly Ad","author":"Camille Caldera","published_date":"2020-10-27T22:49:09Z","latency_ms":442.52802499977406,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}